![](/guides/img/owner-15-profile-desktop-874dd23d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 872; address: carmacars.ca/owner/profile; pins: 1 12.2 84.7, 2 73.4 21.2")

## Texts or email

On **Account** > **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both**: new bookings, payouts, invoices and documents to sign by a short text with a link. Texts need a phone you verified with a code. Statements, invoices and signed documents are always emailed too. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.

## Take a car out of the program

You give 30 days'' notice for that car only. Your other cars stay in.

1. Open Vehicles and the car. Read Leaving: when the notice ends and what happens to your last fees.
2. Press **Give notice**. Add a Reason (optional).
3. Press **Give exit notice**. The car''s page then shows its exit date.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer when one of your cars is booked, when a booking changes, for payouts and payments, incidents and documents to sign.

1. Open **Profile**. Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications when your browser asks.
2. Under **What to alert me about**, choose the topics. Your choice applies to all your devices.
3. **Send a test alert** shows one. **Turn off on this device** stops them there; **Remove** takes another device off.

On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**), then open it from there and turn alerts on. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Keep your details up to date, read our notices, and know how to take a car out of the program.</p><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-notifications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Notifications</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Notifications lists our messages: new bookings, changes to a booking, payments and listing news.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as read</b> on one, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as read</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/notifications</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/692"><img src="/guides/img/owner-14-notifications-desktop-8e58b95e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="692"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.1%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-your-profile" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your profile</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Update your email, phone and address, then press Save.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On your agreements shows your legal name and how you are enrolled. A change to these means new agreements, so call or message us.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/profile</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/872"><img src="/guides/img/owner-15-profile-desktop-874dd23d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="872"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.2%;top:84.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.4%;top:21.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-texts-or-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts or email</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>: new bookings, payouts, invoices and documents to sign by a short text with a link. Texts need a phone you verified with a code. Statements, invoices and signed documents are always emailed too. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-take-a-car-out-of-the-program" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take a car out of the program</h2><p class="gd-p">You give 30 days&#39; notice for that car only. Your other cars stay in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Vehicles and the car. Read Leaving: when the notice ends and what happens to your last fees.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give notice</b>. Add a Reason (optional).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give exit notice</b>. The car&#39;s page then shows its exit date.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer when one of your cars is booked, when a booking changes, for payouts and payments, incidents and documents to sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications when your browser asks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>, choose the topics. Your choice applies to all your devices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> shows one. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off on this device</b> stops them there; <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes another device off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>), then open it from there and turn alerts on. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', 'chapter', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'Every renter, owner, investor and staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## Who gets what

- **Email**: emails only. **Text**: a short text instead of the email. **Both**: a text and the email.
- Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.
- No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.
- Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.
- Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, "Continue your request") are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).
- An additional driver''s or a co-signer''s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.

## A person''s channel

Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card **How we reach them** shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press **Change** to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter''s or owner''s; an investor''s only Admins.

## STOP, START and quiet hours

- A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.
- Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), "CarmaCars: you''re unsubscribed and won''t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe." after STOP, and "CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out." after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.
- The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends "Reply STOP to opt out."
- Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.
- A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.

## The settings and the texts

**Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email''s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.

## Texts a day

Site health on **To do** has **Texts today**: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.
', 'Text alerts: email, text or both', 'Each person''s channel, what is always emailed, STOP and START, quiet hours, US numbers, the texts and the daily count.',
  'Every renter, owner, investor and staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## Who gets what

- **Email**: emails only. **Text**: a short text instead of the email. **Both**: a text and the email.
- Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.
- No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.
- Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.
- Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, "Continue your request") are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).
- An additional driver''s or a co-signer''s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.

## A person''s channel

Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card **How we reach them** shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press **Change** to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter''s or owner''s; an investor''s only Admins.

## STOP, START and quiet hours

- A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.
- Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), "CarmaCars: you''re unsubscribed and won''t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe." after STOP, and "CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out." after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.
- The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends "Reply STOP to opt out."
- Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.
- A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.

## The settings and the texts

**Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email''s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.

## Texts a day

Site health on **To do** has **Texts today**: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.

## Phone alerts

Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**; iOS 16.4 or later).

- What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts.
- Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.
- Your own: **Settings** > **My phone alerts**.
- On or off for everyone: **Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**, "Phone alerts".
- Setup: alerts need two keys in the vault, `deploy_vapid_public_key` and `deploy_vapid_private_key`. Until they are there the cards are hidden and **My phone alerts** says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.
',
